    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1004">

                <pb facs="1164" n="968" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg968"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.515/8–245: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1004<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of the Division of Economic
                        Security Controls</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Rubin</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Chief of the Division of Economic Security
                        Controls</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Oliver</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1004-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-08-02">August 2, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Victory</hi> 480. For Oliver from Rubin.</p>
                <p>President has sent to General Clay memo<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1004-f2"/> stating
                    agreement of Big Three to issuance of decree vesting German foreign assets, and
                    directing that ACC (Allied Control Commission) be urged to adopt decree. Memo
                    states that President regards it as urgent that control and power of disposition
                    over German external assets be obtained. Draft of decree already sent to
                        you<anchor n="3" xml:id="d1004-f3"/> has been amended by striking <pb
                        facs="1165" n="969" xml:id="pg969"/> portion which previously set up a
                    special board (with US and UK represented) to direct the vesting body.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1004-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1004-f1-content">
